<figure class="setup-howto" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
  <ol class="howto-steps">
    <li class="howto-step">
      <p><span class="howto-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><strong>Get Cueport for Mac.</strong> Install the app on your Mac.</p>
      {%- if product.apps.mac.downloadUrl %}
      <a class="setup-download setup-download--live" href="{{ product.apps.mac.downloadUrl }}">Download for Mac</a>
      {%- else %}
      <span class="setup-download" role="button" aria-disabled="true"><span>Download for Mac</span><span class="setup-download-soon">Coming soon</span></span>
      {%- endif %}
    </li>
    <li class="howto-step">
      <p><span class="howto-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><strong>Choose a library.</strong></p>
      <p class="howto-choice"><span class="howto-tag" aria-hidden="true">A</span><strong>Serato library.</strong> Use your <code>_Serato_</code> folder to build your library.</p>
      <p class="howto-choice"><span class="howto-tag" aria-hidden="true">B</span><strong>Cueport Direct.</strong> Build your library directly from your music files. <a class="trailmix-link" href="https://trailmix.tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">trail mix <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a> analyzes locally.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="howto-step">
      <p><span class="howto-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><strong>Get the Cueport app.</strong> Sync selected or all collections to your phone.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption class="setup-caption">The iPhone app will be available through the App Store.</figcaption>
</figure>
